WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.602
Marguerite signs in.

2
00:00:01.926 --> 00:00:06.139
Pillar-43 runs on this laptop, with a small local model.

3
00:00:06.463 --> 00:00:13.452
The screen lists thirteen items open to the AI: contracts, design, catalog, letters, minutes.

4
00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:22.556
She types a question in plain words: where are we allowed to sell the Lanterns book, and is it paperback only?

5
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.897
While the model works, a Stop button sits beside the question.

6
00:00:27.221 --> 00:00:31.164
The answer has to point at a passage the archive holds.

7
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:39.311
The answer quotes the grant clause: English language, the United States and its territories, paperback.

8
00:00:39.635 --> 00:00:45.338
On the right it lists what it could not see, items closed by their writers.

9
00:00:45.662 --> 00:00:51.269
She clicks the citation, and the contract opens with that clause highlighted.

10
00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:53.860
She opens the whole file.

11
00:00:54.184 --> 00:01:02.026
It sits in the file tree among the press's contracts, board minutes and letters, open at the same page.

12
00:01:05.066 --> 00:01:10.297
Tomasz, the translator, opens My work, a screen that lists only his items.

13
00:01:10.621 --> 00:01:17.414
He sets his Lanterns contract from Model to Staff: staff can still open it, the AI can't.

14
00:01:17.738 --> 00:01:19.987
Ines signs in and asks the same question.

15
00:01:20.311 --> 00:01:26.973
The answer is declined: its writer closed this contract, so the AI did not read it.

16
00:01:27.297 --> 00:01:34.120
A contract set to Private would not appear to staff at all; the archive would only count it.

17
00:01:35.165 --> 00:01:37.558
In Explore, she searches for yellow.

18
00:01:37.882 --> 00:01:43.353
A timeline shows one row per title, and a dot for each document at its date.

19
00:01:43.678 --> 00:01:47.939
She opens a dot: a design note on the yellow reissue cover.

20
00:01:48.263 --> 00:01:52.575
In People, Cassia Merrowby's record lists her titles and dates.

21
00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:55.375
Closed items are counted, never shown.

22
00:01:56.398 --> 00:02:01.989
Back in Files, everything is where the press left it: nothing re-filed or summarised.

23
00:02:02.313 --> 00:02:07.574
The code is open, at github.com/caerjar/pillar-43.
